BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Myth & Archetype as seen through Poetry & Astrology
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260913T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260913T170000
UID:6a5eda868a9917634a5f60d8@squarespace.com
DESCRIPTION:We invite all to a fascinating afternoon with Diana and Brian 
 who will explore through the respective lenses of astrology and poetry\, v
 aluable insights offered by both myth and archetype\, for better clarity a
 nd resilience in today’s tumultuous world.\nThis event features Author a
 nd Astrologer Diana Badger discussing her book "\nDance of the Archetypes:
  How Astrology Informs our Lives and Connects Us to the Earth"\,\nand Auth
 or/Poet/Storyteller Brian R. Martens with his book\,\n"Merlin’s Wing"\, 
 Mythic Poems.\nThis event is free\, all donations gratefully invited. Sele
 cted readings from each presenter\, a storytelling with Brian\, then Q&A\,
  book sales & signing\n.\nRefreshments for sale. OCA’s facilities are ac
 cessible to people with disabilities.\nDance of the Archetypes\nby Diana B
 adger\nWhether you’re new to astrology or already immersed in its symbol
 ism\,\nDance of the Archetypes\nilluminates the zodiac in a refreshingly a
 ccessible way. With grounded wisdom\, Diana connects planetary cycles to t
 he Earth we depend on\, our emotional lives\, and our healing. This is a b
 eautifully integrative guide for readers seeking relevance\, connection\, 
 and purpose in rapidly changing times\, brought to life by the author’s 
 own striking photographs.\nFor the past 20 years\, Diana Badger has woven 
 together parallel careers as a counseling astrologer and a writer/editor\,
  while pursuing an ongoing commitment to inner work and spiritual practice
 . Rooted in a reverence for the natural world and informed by multiple wis
 dom traditions\, Diana’s work reflects a lifelong inquiry into the relat
 ionship between psyche\, cosmos\, and Earth. She currently devotes her tim
 e to her\nEarth Sky Journal\npodcast/writing\, her astrology practice\, te
 nding of her garden\, and adventures in local community.\nMerlin’s Wing\
 nby Brian Martens\nThis collection of poems is concerned with the “Human
  Condition” : Awareness\, Transformation\, and Deep Intuition. His poetr
 y resonates with yearning\, humor and intelligence in which he expresses h
 is love and admiration for the first people\, the ancestors\, animal\, hum
 an and plant. He asks these voices to speak through him in symbols\, rhyth
 ms and revelations to reveal the deep beauty\, tragedy\, and unknowable my
 stery that surrounds him.\nBrian R. Martens is an abstract Artist\, Poet\,
  Author\, Creativity Facilitator\, International Speaker\, Myth Maker\, CA
  Poets in the Schools Instructor\, Podcaster\, and Storyteller. Brian weav
 es poetry\, myth\, and reflection into all his storytelling. His first boo
 k\,\nThree Raven Gate\n\, is a collection of haiku\, the form he learned f
 rom his work with Angeles Arrien Ph.D.\, a cross-cultural anthropologist\,
  over the course of seven years. Brian seeks to inspire and motivate peopl
 e\, with articles\, podcasts\, creativity workshops\, and poetry to recogn
 ize their own deep creative spirit and to express that to the world.
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts\, 3850 Doris Murphy Court\, Occide
 ntal\, CA 95465
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/myth-archet
 ype-as-seen-through-poetry-astrology
X-SOURCE:Occidental Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
